.TH EUCLID-CLI-ESM-MOVE-OBJECT 1 "September 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.33" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-esm-move-object \- move an object to another key or bucket
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli esm move-object
.BR \-\-source\-bucket | \-b
.I ERN
.BR \-\-source\-key | \-k
.I KEY
.BR \-\-target\-key | \-K
.I KEY
[\fB\-\-target\-bucket\fR|\fB\-B\fR \fIERN\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Moves an object to another key, in the same bucket or a different one.
.PP
Nothing is copied. An object's bytes live in a file named after an
internal identifier, and only the database says which key that file
answers to - so a move is a change of key, and costs the same whether the
object is a kilobyte or a hundred gigabytes. The object keeps its content
type, checksum and attributes; it gets a new ERN, since an ERN names a
bucket and a key.
.PP
Both buckets are checked against the caller's account and, for a caller
with resource grants, against those grants.
.PP
Anything subscribed to the target bucket is notified that an object
appeared there, which is what happened as far as a subscriber is
concerned, however it arrived.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-source\-bucket " " \fIERN\fR
Euclid resource name of the bucket the object is in. Required.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-source\-key " " \fIKEY\fR
Key of the object within that bucket. Required.
.TP
.BR \-K ", " \-\-target\-key " " \fIKEY\fR
Key it should have. Required.
.TP
.BR \-B ", " \-\-target\-bucket " " \fIERN\fR
Bucket it should end up in. Defaults to the source bucket, which makes
this a rename - see
.BR euclid-cli-esm-rename-object (1).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The object was moved. It is printed as JSON, in its new place.
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, no session, either bucket does not exist or
belongs to another account, the source object does not exist, or
something is already stored at the target key.
.SH EXAMPLES
Move a processed file out of an inbox:
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli esm move-object \e
    --source-bucket ern:esm:eu-central-1:000000000000::bucket:inbox \e
    --source-key report.csv \e
    --target-bucket ern:esm:eu-central-1:000000000000::bucket:processed \e
    --target-key report.csv
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-esm (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-copy-object (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-rename-object (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-delete-object (1)
